# Design system

Read the brief, current UI, existing `PRODUCT.md` and `DESIGN.md` if present. Establish audience, brand constraints, content hierarchy, accessibility needs, and primary interface states. Propose actual color, spacing, typography, and component tokens; use verified font families and real values, not placeholders. Explain tradeoffs among a few coherent looks when the direction is unsettled. A settled user choice is an input, not a reason to ask again.

Prepare a reviewable proposal and preview. Write `DESIGN.md` at the requested location or the project's existing design path only when that write is within scope. Preserve a kept legacy document and avoid overwriting user content. Validate a new spec with `gstack-design-md.ts check DESIGN.md` and report the detected format. If a project instruction file must be updated to point to the design system, edit that file deliberately and preserve its existing rules. Stop with the design artifact and preview evidence; implementation is a separate step.

